<title>USA: Omnicom Group buys Cline, Davis &amp; Mann - NYT.</title>
<headline>Omnicom Group buys Cline, Davis &amp; Mann - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Omnicom Group is expanding into health care advertising by acquiring New York agency Cline, Davis &amp; Mann, the New York Times said Thursday.</p>
<p>The paper said terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The report said Omnicom is the world's second largest agency with billings estimated at $20.2 billion. It said Cline, Davis has nearly 170 employees and billings estimated at $170 million.</p>
<p>The report said Cline, Davis' clients include pharmaceutical marketers such as Pfizer Inc and the Parke-Davis division of Warner-Lambert Co.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
